  "ai_summary": "IT consultancy stocks crashed another 24% in 30 days, compounding a 34% annual drop as investors price in AI automation for outsourced work. Meanwhile, Indeed postings rose 18% year-over-year despite a slowing 2.8% 30-day gain, echoing flat Big Tech headcounts (-2.9% YoY). AI labs boast massive yearly job growth (+215%), though recent momentum cools. Devs aren't universally cooked, but low-tier outsourcing faces imminent AI displacement. Watching consultancy stocks plummet another 24% in a month makes you realize that \"digital transformation\" really just meant transforming digital workers into unemployment statistics.",
